Scoped Qwen4exp graph and HIP optimizations following the selected-key kernel patch.
Adapted from the MIT-licensed halo-box/strix-llama.cpp snapshot
7a9196dad8b13b70fb3420886aadaf98fc09b849.
https://github.com/halo-box/strix-llama.cpp/commit/7a9196dad8b13b70fb3420886aadaf98fc09b849

The compact graph requires PARACETAMOL_QWEN4EXP_QSA_GRAPH=1 and the existing
selected-key kernel opt-in. Only a unique scalar prefix with supported F16
attention geometry uses it. Other cache layouts retain the ordinary graph.
Whole-block selection follows the reference block budget plus partial tail.
Maskless selected IDs have explicit CPU semantics and are rejected by GPU
backends without support. Scorer strips, ordered F32 pooling/head-sum fusions,
and explicitly hinted Qwen4exp matrix operations avoid global kernel changes.
The HIP optimizations dispatch only on gfx1151. No BF16 shadow weights,
residual downcasts, persistent derived KV state, or allocation-policy change.

